(a) All members of the Board of Ethics shall serve a four-year term. The members shall elect a chair and develop their own organization internally.
(b) The position of a member of the board shall be deemed vacated:
(1) Upon the expiration of his or her term;
(2) Upon the death of a member or the disability or incapacity of a member for more than 90 days;
(3) Upon the written resignation of the member;
(4) By the member ceasing to be a resident of the city;
(5) Upon qualifying for a political office within the City of Riverdale; or
(6) Upon removal of the member for good cause by a majority vote of the board of ethics.
(c) If a vacancy occurs, new members shall be identified and their names submitted to the municipal clerk within 30 days of the date on which a vacancy in a board position occurs. The municipal clerk will sound their names at the next regularly scheduled council meeting to be voted on by the city council unless a mayor appointee who does not require a majority vote.
(d) Members of the board of ethics may be removed by majority vote of the city governing authority.
(Ord. No. 12-2016, § 1, 7-11-16; Ord. No. 1 [2017], § 1, 8-4-17)

